the peaches and the pecans.

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:38.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, I did not even put it
together. There you go.

00:00:38.238 --> 00:00:39.472
-They really make a nice combo.

00:00:39.472 --> 00:00:40.940 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, cheers to the combo,
guys.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:44.444 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Cheers to that. Heck, yeah.
-This is great.

00:00:44.444 --> 00:00:45.845 align:start size:94% position:6%
It´s great.
I said it before I drank it.

00:00:45.845 --> 00:00:47.047 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wow!
-So I want to say it again.

00:00:47.047 --> 00:00:48.214 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:49.549 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is great, seriously.
You should buy some.

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:50.784 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It´s really good.
You should all buy some.

00:00:50.784 --> 00:00:53.219
So, you guys have been the road.

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:54.821
You´re doing the Smooth tour.

00:00:54.821 --> 00:00:57.223 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you enjoy being out on
the road playing to your fans?

00:00:57.223 --> 00:00:58.358 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We do, man.
-Absolutely.

00:00:58.358 --> 00:00:59.759 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That´s probably
one of our favorite things,

00:00:59.759 --> 00:01:01.594 size:78% position:39%
really being on tour,
being on the stage,

00:01:01.594 --> 00:01:02.962
connecting with the fans.

00:01:02.962 --> 00:01:05.365
Getting to kind of create
the vision and, you know,

00:01:05.365 --> 00:01:07.500 align:start size:94% position:6%
create the show and watch it
come to life every night.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:08.535 align:start size:94% position:6%
Man, it´s unreal.

00:01:08.535 --> 00:01:09.936 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You have different acts
touring with you,

00:01:09.936 --> 00:01:12.305 align:start size:94% position:6%
and some of them are I think
what you would consider

00:01:12.305 --> 00:01:13.373
conventional country acts,

00:01:13.373 --> 00:01:15.075 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you also have
some different genres.

00:01:15.075 --> 00:01:17.177 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is it true that Nelly has been
on tour with you guys?

00:01:17.177 --> 00:01:19.813
-We got Nelly out with us.
We got the Backstreet Boys.

00:01:19.813 --> 00:01:21.548 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The Backstreet Boys?
That´s fantastic.

00:01:21.548 --> 00:01:23.783 size:75% position:38%
-Mixing some genres,
crossing some lines.

00:01:23.783 --> 00:01:26.352
-And are there times where
you look out and you say,

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:28.621
"Oh, I think there are people
here that would not be here

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:31.291 align:start size:94% position:6%
if it wasn´t for
the Backstreet Boys or Nelly?"

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:33.960 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh...
You know what?

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:35.161 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yes and no.

00:01:35.161 --> 00:01:37.764 size:88% position:44%
I mean, our fan base is
pretty diverse, as well.

00:01:37.764 --> 00:01:39.232
But it is cool. I mean it´s --

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:43.670
it´s wild to see country music
fans going nuts for two hours

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:45.905
before we hit the stage
for Nelly and Backstreet,

00:01:45.905 --> 00:01:47.240
and it´s really a cool vibe.

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:50.043
-Now, were you guys
Backstreet Boys fans growing up?

00:01:50.043 --> 00:01:51.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Dude, they were
my first concert.

00:01:51.377 --> 00:01:53.813 align:start size:94% position:6%
Sixth grade, House of Blues,
Orlando, Florida.

00:01:53.813 --> 00:01:56.349 align:start size:94% position:6%
I´ll never forget.
-That´s fantastic.

00:01:56.349 --> 00:01:58.118
-Full circle.
-I would definitely bust on you

00:01:58.118 --> 00:01:59.986 align:start size:94% position:6%
if Vanilla Ice
wasn´t my first concert.

00:01:59.986 --> 00:02:01.321 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes!
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.321 --> 00:02:03.523 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That´s a good one.
-So who am I to judge?

00:02:03.523 --> 00:02:05.058 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That´s a great one.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:05.058 --> 00:02:06.926
Now he´s flipping houses on TV.

00:02:06.926 --> 00:02:08.761 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, so he´s doing great.
-He´s killing it.

00:02:08.761 --> 00:02:10.363 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Ice is doing great.
-He´s killing it.

00:02:10.363 --> 00:02:13.133 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You guys --
you did Wrigley Field.

00:02:13.133 --> 00:02:14.400 align:start size:94% position:6%
How was that?

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:16.402
How was performing Wrigley Field
for a concert venue?

00:02:16.402 --> 00:02:17.837 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That was a dream come true.
-Yes.

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:19.873
-I mean, absolutely amazing.

00:02:19.873 --> 00:02:23.109 align:start size:94% position:6%
It sold out, so that alone was
amazing and then, I mean,

00:02:23.109 --> 00:02:25.111 align:start size:94% position:6%
the fans in Chicago,
we love Chicago.

00:02:25.111 --> 00:02:29.349
I mean, their energy is electric
and it was a special night.

00:02:29.349 --> 00:02:31.718 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Were you drafted to play
in the majors?

00:02:31.718 --> 00:02:33.987
-I wasn´t drafted, but I played
baseball all through college.

00:02:33.987 --> 00:02:36.055 align:start size:94% position:6%
I played in
three different colleges.

00:02:36.055 --> 00:02:38.291 align:start size:94% position:6%
Florida State for two years,
Daytona State College,

00:02:38.291 --> 00:02:40.493 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then Belmont for my last
two years of eligibility.

00:02:40.493 --> 00:02:43.196
So it was a dream at one point,
but music took over,

00:02:43.196 --> 00:02:46.499
and pretty cool to play
our songs in a baseball stadium.

00:02:46.499 --> 00:02:47.901 size:84% position:42%
Wrigley, Fenway. Crazy.

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:50.803 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It´s, like, the one thing
that´s harder to do at Wrigley

00:02:50.803 --> 00:02:53.406 align:start size:94% position:6%
than play baseball
is play a concert.

00:02:53.406 --> 00:02:55.141 size:84% position:42%
Like, you did the thing
that has actually had

00:02:55.141 --> 00:02:56.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
the odds stacked against you
more than that.

00:02:56.676 --> 00:02:58.178 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It´s crazy. Yeah.
-So congratulations on that.

00:02:58.178 --> 00:02:59.479 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you.
We´re super blessed.

00:02:59.479 --> 00:03:02.148 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I want to ask about this.
Whose house has this --

00:03:02.148 --> 00:03:03.316 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is a treehouse
that one of you has.

00:03:03.316 --> 00:03:04.684 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is this yours?

00:03:04.684 --> 00:03:06.819
-My wife and I have a cool
little spot out in the woods

00:03:06.819 --> 00:03:07.987 size:78% position:39%
outside of Nashville.

00:03:07.987 --> 00:03:09.689 size:88% position:44%
And we got Pete Nelson
from "Treehouse Masters"

00:03:09.689 --> 00:03:10.723
build us a little tree house.

00:03:10.723 --> 00:03:11.891 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There´s a guy --

00:03:11.891 --> 00:03:12.959 size:81% position:41%
There´s a place called
"Treehouse Masters"?

00:03:12.959 --> 00:03:14.227 align:start size:94% position:6%
-On TV, yeah.
-Oh, wow!

00:03:14.227 --> 00:03:15.295 align:start size:94% position:6%
-A TV show, yeah.

00:03:15.295 --> 00:03:17.497 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It´s a TV -- Oh.
-Where have you been?

00:03:17.497 --> 00:03:19.732
-Well, obviously you watch
a lot of real-estate shows.

00:03:19.732 --> 00:03:21.234
You´re telling me about Vanilla
Ice and now the treehouse guy.

00:03:21.234 --> 00:03:22.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:22.368 --> 00:03:24.037 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, I have a problem with
real estate.

00:03:24.037 --> 00:03:25.438 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.

00:03:25.438 --> 00:03:27.407 align:start size:94% position:6%
I like to just pour
my peach pecan whiskey

00:03:27.407 --> 00:03:28.775
and just watch some houses.

00:03:28.775 --> 00:03:31.077
-Check on some Trulia, man.
Just check on some Zillow.

00:03:31.077 --> 00:03:33.479 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is gorgeous. What do you
do in your treehouse?

00:03:33.479 --> 00:03:35.215 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, we have
a little recording studio.

00:03:35.215 --> 00:03:36.349 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That´s fantastic.

00:03:36.349 --> 00:03:37.884 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It´s a creative space
so we write songs,

00:03:37.884 --> 00:03:40.720
recorded a lot of vocals for our
"Dig Your Roots," last album.

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:41.988 size:88% position:44%
Just a cool space. Yeah.

00:03:41.988 --> 00:03:43.756 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I would say
this looks like a really --

00:03:43.756 --> 00:03:46.259
I mean, it does look like a
place I would want to hang out.

00:03:46.259 --> 00:03:48.228
-The fact that it´s like
15 minutes from downtown,

00:03:48.228 --> 00:03:50.430
we can just jump over and kind
of get away out in the woods.

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:52.932
-That really speaks to what
a great place Nashville is,

00:03:52.932 --> 00:03:54.867 align:start size:94% position:6%
that this is 15 minutes
from downtown

00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:57.003 align:start size:94% position:6%
because 15 minutes from here
does not look like this.

00:03:57.003 --> 00:03:58.571 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Not quite. Not quite, no.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:58.571 --> 00:04:00.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You have to go a lot farther
from New York.

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:02.976
You can find apartments that are
as big as this treehouse.

00:04:02.976 --> 00:04:05.311
-We´re thinking about building
one in Central Park, actually.

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:07.480 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ] Great, yeah.
-Still working on that permit.

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:09.582 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There probably are some weird
treehouses in Central Park

00:04:09.582 --> 00:04:12.252 align:start size:94% position:6%
that the police have just
decided to let be.

00:04:12.252 --> 00:04:13.953 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:13.953 --> 00:04:15.989 size:78% position:39%
Now, you´re -- you´re
about to have a baby?

00:04:15.989 --> 00:04:17.323
-Yes, we are. Yes, we are, yeah.

00:04:17.323 --> 00:04:18.858 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That´s fantastic.
Congratulations.

00:04:18.858 --> 00:04:20.627 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you very much.
December 20th.

00:04:20.627 --> 00:04:21.661 align:start size:94% position:6%
-December 20th. Whoo!
-Thank you.

00:04:21.661 --> 00:04:23.129 size:84% position:42%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:23.129 --> 00:04:27.734
-So you -- you know what you´re
having but you got it wrong?

00:04:27.734 --> 00:04:29.802 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We had it wrong. We did.
-Okay.

00:04:29.802 --> 00:04:31.871 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Apparently, that is possible.
-Yeah.

00:04:31.871 --> 00:04:34.307 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, we had -- the blood test
was actually incorrect.

00:04:34.307 --> 00:04:37.110
We went and got the ultrasound
done, like, the big ultrasound

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:38.611 align:start size:94% position:6%
at, like, five months
or whatever.

00:04:38.611 --> 00:04:41.314
So for two and a half months
we thought we were having a boy.

00:04:41.314 --> 00:04:43.850 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And we were excited.

00:04:43.850 --> 00:04:47.020 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then gears kind of shifted
for about a day and a half,

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:49.188
and it was a new surprise.

00:04:49.188 --> 00:04:51.691
But it was something that
we´re both really excited about.

00:04:51.691 --> 00:04:53.293 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think
it´s going to be amazing.

00:04:53.293 --> 00:04:55.161 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It´s great.
Having just gone through it,

00:04:55.161 --> 00:04:56.829
it is one of those things
when you find out the sex.

00:04:56.829 --> 00:04:58.931 size:81% position:41%
You think, you know --

00:04:58.931 --> 00:05:01.000 align:start size:94% position:6%
you realize
they´re each super exciting.

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:02.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
-For sure.
-There´s no outside output --

00:05:02.835 --> 00:05:04.804 align:start size:94% position:6%
-In different ways,
though, you know?

00:05:04.804 --> 00:05:06.072 align:start size:94% position:6%
You kind of got to definitely
shift gears.

00:05:06.072 --> 00:05:08.174 align:start size:94% position:6%
But give me some --
You got any fatherly advice?

00:05:08.174 --> 00:05:10.243
-I mean, the only thing I´ll say
is for the first year

00:05:10.243 --> 00:05:13.112
just never complain about
anything <i>you </i>have to do.

00:05:13.112 --> 00:05:14.113 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:14.113 --> 00:05:15.581 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Own it.
-It´s, like, no matter --

00:05:15.581 --> 00:05:16.749
if there´s a where you´re like,

00:05:16.749 --> 00:05:19.285
"This is my third diaper
in a row," just eat that.

00:05:19.285 --> 00:05:21.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, just don´t --
-Literally.

00:05:21.254 --> 00:05:22.555 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Because they really,
like, it --

00:05:22.555 --> 00:05:24.957 align:start size:94% position:6%
I feel like it´s probably,
like 20, 25 years

00:05:24.957 --> 00:05:26.392 align:start size:94% position:6%
before you can even
begin to catch up

00:05:26.392 --> 00:05:28.094 align:start size:94% position:6%
as far as how much
the mother has to do.

00:05:28.094 --> 00:05:29.228 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I understand.
-Yeah.

00:05:29.228 --> 00:05:30.697
-Props to them, I will say that.
-Absolutely.

00:05:30.697 --> 00:05:32.131 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, thanks, guys,
for being here.

00:05:32.131 --> 00:05:34.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
I can´t wait to hear the song,
and I really appreciate it.

00:05:34.434 --> 00:05:35.735 size:84% position:42%
Thanks for the whiskey.

00:05:35.735 --> 00:05:37.804 align:start size:94% position:6%
Brian Kelley and Tyler Hubbard
of Florida Georgia Line!

